I've been absent for a while from this nice community, sadly, because of
the university, work...

However, I'm going to do something I was planning about half a year:
give a talk in a sort of convention. It's called "Jornadas del Sur"
(something like {snanu gunka djedi}), and it's mostly about free
software, and free culture.

"Jornadas del Sur" is going to be held this weekend (Saturday, Sunday
and Monday, which here in Argentina it's holiday), and my talk will be
held, if nothing strange happen in between, on Monday, at 10 am (GMT
-3). (And I'm a little bit nervous... :x)

This was just to let you know that I'm still here, willing to be useful
to Lojban (and learn it, of course).

If you are interested, I can give you more information, or the slides
(which are going to be under Creative Commons licence).

